# Perspective calibration room

Status: DONE
Milestone: M1 visual environment
Dependencies: 04_SYNTHETIC_STAGE.todo, 11_REFERENCE_AVATAR.todo

## Purpose
Make the existing reference character feel situated in a test lab with proper room perspective,
following the two supplied room examples rather than replacing it with the example mannequin.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect both supplied room references and retain original hashes/private copies.
- [x] Implement projected floor, ceiling, side walls and back wall with coherent grid/markers.
- [x] Add conservative visual shoe shadows; preserve tracking, avatar, crop/loss and mirror behavior.
- [x] Keep the room toggle and clean-output behavior usable across aspect ratios.
- [x] Inspect/test projection, shadows, actual runtime, docs and evidence.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Visible room enclosure and shared perspective vanishing point, not a flat grid.
- [x] Existing character/motion/expressions and synthetic-only boundary remain intact.
- [x] No collision, real-room calibration, missing-foot reconstruction or interaction claims.

